{"diagnosis": "Recent repair-family runs show that increasing recurrence depth and verifier-call count collapses exactness on shallow/layered families: cycles=2+rlt dropped to 0.5176 and latent_steps=3+verifier_visits=2+visits=4 dropped to 0.498, both far below the ~0.97-1.0 incumbent behavior, while ldt_projection only cost ~0.01 (0.9688 vs 0.978). Interpretation: on shallow layered tasks the answer update is not the bottleneck; the RLT coefficient eta=1/(D-u) grows as u approaches D and destabilizes the recurrent answer state, and extra verifier calls/visits add variance without adding signal. Direct feedback with shallow depth is the robust regime. The retrieval incumbent (dev_exact 1.0, 3 visits, 1 verifier call, 11683 params, ~3.35M FLOPs) is therefore already at the accuracy ceiling; the remaining lever is FLOPs/visit reduction and stable training signal, not more capacity.",
  "proposals": [
    {"config": {"visits": 2}, "rationale": "Exact transitive dependency sets on layered_shallow need direct-dependency selection plus one verifier frontier pass; a third visit adds ~1/3 of the per-visit FLOPs for marginal supervision. FLOPs/instance scale roughly linearly in visits, so 3->2 cuts ~33% inference cost while preserving the direct->verifier->answer pipeline.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.99, "falsification": "dev_exact < 0.99 or exact_by_visit[0] < 1.0 (i.e., the first visit no longer recovers the full dependency set)."},
    {"config": {"feedback": "matched_damping"}, "rationale": "Keeps the damped answer update (y <- y + eta(e-y)) but with constant eta whose coefficient sum matches RLT, avoiding RLT's eta=1/(D-u) blow-up as u->D that likely caused the 0.5176 failure. Inference graph and FLOPs are unchanged from the incumbent; only the answer-update gain changes.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.99, "falsification": "dev_exact < 0.99 or ece worse than incumbent's ~0.0005, indicating the damped gain does not help on this family."},
    {"config": {"grad_cycles": 2}, "rationale": "Gradient through 2 cycles improves credit assignment into the latent step without increasing inference FLOPs (cycles stays 1) or params; deep supervision across visits already provides the final-visit signal, so the extra backward pass mainly sharpens the last-cycle gradient.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.995, "falsification": "dev_exact < 0.99 or train_seconds/peak_rss materially worse with no exact gain, indicating the extra backward cycle only adds cost."}
  ]}
